# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — Temporary Trivy suppressions
# =============================================================================
#
# Rules:
#   1. Every entry MUST have an expiration date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD).
#   2. Every entry MUST link to an upstream tracking issue/advisory.
#   3. When an entry expires, re-evaluate: remove it if the CVE is fixed,
#      or extend the date with a new justification if the fix still isn't
#      available. Never extend without re-checking upstream.
#   4. Keep the file short. A growing ignorefile is a smell.
#   5. Verify against the pinned CI Trivy (TRIVY_VERSION in security.yml /
#      cve-scan.yml) and its DB source — local `brew install trivy` uses
#      the ghcr.io DB which can classify severities differently from the
#      CI's mirror.gcr.io/aquasec/trivy-db:2.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# =============================================================================

# CVE-2026-48863, CVE-2026-48864, CVE-2026-9149, CVE-2026-9150 — libsolv
# buffer overflows in the AL2023 package shipped by the
# public.ecr.aws/lambda/python:3.14 base image used by the helm-installer
# Lambda. Installed 0.7.22-1.amzn2023.0.3; fixed in 0.7.22-1.amzn2023.0.4
# per the Amazon Linux 2023 advisory (https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2023/).
#
# The fix is published, but only in an AL2023 releasever newer than the one
# the base image pins, so it can't be pulled without floating the package.
# We're waiting for AWS to refresh the Lambda Python 3.14 base image with
# the rebuilt libsolv rather than patching at build time. Low runtime risk:
# libsolv is dnf's SAT solver, exercised only at image build, never by the
# running Lambda. Clears when AWS refreshes the base image.
CVE-2026-48863 exp:2026-09-12
CVE-2026-48864 exp:2026-09-12
CVE-2026-9149 exp:2026-09-12
CVE-2026-9150 exp:2026-09-12

# CVE-2026-12151 — undici (Node.js) Denial of Service via unbounded memory
# growth on the WebSocket client. undici is not a tracked or shipped GCO
# dependency: no package.json is committed in the repo, and it is pulled in
# transitively only by Node tooling in the CI environment. GCO ships no Node
# service and uses no undici WebSocket client, so the DoS path is never
# exercised at runtime. Fixed upstream in undici 6.27.0 / 7.28.0 / 8.5.0;
# clears when the CI tool that bundles undici refreshes its pin.
# Advisory: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-12151
CVE-2026-12151 exp:2026-09-21
